{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Interactions.qbeta_tower_bound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Interactions.qbeta_tower_bound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.residual_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.residual_pos","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_tower_bound.lean#L53-L58","doc":"**Residual is positive and monotone in `x`.** For `0 < x < 1` the relative\n`N=0` truncation residual `x/(1−x)` is positive — the resummed scale is\nalways above the single-tick value, so the `N=0` form under-predicts and\nthe residual has a definite sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.E0_tower_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.E0_tower_gap","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_tower_bound.lean#L44-L51","doc":"**Energy-scale tower residual.** With `x = (ℏ_q^E)²` the per-level factor,\nthe resummed energy scale `𝔈₀/(1−x)` exceeds the `N=0` value `𝔈₀` by\nexactly `𝔈₀·x/(1−x)` — the closed bound on the truncation residual that\nthe `+0.17%` Q_β agreement sits inside. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.counit_dominates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.counit_dominates","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_tower_bound.lean#L33-L42","doc":"**Dominance.** At the substrate (`h > 0`, `h < 2z`, `z < 1`) both values\nare negative and the counit is the more negative, so the counit dominates\nin magnitude: `|ε(Δ)| > |tr_M(Δ)|`. This is exactly why the counit form\nreaches `Q_β` while the trace falls short. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.trace_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.trace_neg","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_tower_bound.lean#L27-L31","doc":"**Trace negative at the substrate.** When `h < 2z` the Markov-trace value\non the nucleon difference is negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.counit_lt_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.QBetaTowerBound.counit_lt_trace","kind":"theorem","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Interactions/qbeta_tower_bound.lean#L21-L25","doc":"**Counit below trace.** For `h > 0` and loop `z < 1`, the counit value\nis strictly below the Markov-trace value on the nucleon difference. ","signatureChunk":0}]}